@startuml
title BlueDocs — classes métier et relations Eloquent
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty methods

class User {
  +id: bigint
  +name: string
  +email: string
  +role: string
  +email_verified_at: datetime?
  +last_login_at: datetime?
  +created_at: datetime
  +updated_at: datetime
}

class Document {
  +id: bigint
  +slug: string
  +title: string
  +content: longtext
  +user_name: string
  +updated_by: bigint?
  +created_at: datetime
  +updated_at: datetime
  +editor(): BelongsTo<User>
}

class Section {
  +id: bigint
  +title: string
  +created_at: datetime
  +updated_at: datetime
  +documents(): BelongsToMany<Document>
}

class DocumentSection <<pivot attendu>> {
  +section_id: bigint
  +document_id: bigint
  {primary} section_id, document_id
}

User "0..1" <-- "0..*" Document : updated_by / editor
Document "1" -- "0..*" DocumentSection
Section "1" -- "0..*" DocumentSection

note on link
  La relation many-to-many est déclarée dans les modèles
  et la migration. La table pivot n'a pas été trouvée
  dans la base MySQL observée.
end note

note right of Document
  user_name est une attribution textuelle;
  ce n'est pas une association vers User.
  La migration impose l'unicité du slug,
  mais l'index unique manque dans la
  base MySQL observée.
end note
@enduml
